try>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MASARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA KIYOTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHIHARA, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IBIDEN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MASARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA, KIYOTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>CHIHARA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MASARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA KIYOTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHIHARA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MASARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA, KIYOTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A printed wiring board and method for producing the same, in which an upper-surface pattern is readily formed, and a lower-surface metal foil is hardly damaged when a blind via hole is made by a laser beam. A lower-surface metal foil (220) is provided over the lower surface of an insulating sheet (5), and an upper-surface metal foil (210) thinner than the lower-surface metal foil (220) is provided over its upper surface. An open hole (213) is made in the upper-surface metal foil in a position corresponding to the area (35) where a blind via hole is formed. A laser beam (8) is projected onto the area (35) through the open hole (213) to make a blind via hole (3) the bottom of which is the lower-surface metal foil. A metal plating film (23) is formed on the inner wall of the blind via hole (3). Upper- and lower-surface patterns (21, 22) are formed by etching.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une carte de circuits imprimés ainsi qu'un procédé de fabrication associé, dans lequel on forme auparavant un motif de surface supérieure et on perce un trou borgne au moyen d'un faisceau laser, sans à peine endommager une feuille métallique de surface inférieure. Ce procédé consiste à déposer une feuille métallique de surface inférieure (220) sur la surface inférieure d'une feuille isolante (5), à déposer sur la surface supérieure de cette feuille une feuille métallique de surface supérieure (210), plus mince que la feuille métallique de surface inférieure (220), puis à ménager un trou ouvert (213) dans la feuille métallique de surface supérieure, au niveau d'une position correspondant à la zone (35) de formation du trou borgne, et enfin à projeter un faisceau laser (8) sur ladite zone (35), à travers le trou ouvert (213), afin de ménager un trou borgne (3) dont le fond est constitué par la feuille métallique de surface inférieure. Enfin, le procédé consiste à former un film de placage métallique (23) sur la paroi intérieure du trou borgne (3), des motifs de surface supérieure et inférieure (21, 22) étant formés par gravure.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml 